    VALUES (subj, tid, 'The circuit below is excited by a sinusoidal source. The value of R, in Ω, for which the admittance of the circuit becomes a pure conductance at all...', 'The circuit below is excited by a sinusoidal source. The value of R, in Ω, for which the admittance of the circuit becomes a pure
conductance at all frequencies is _____________.

![Two branches in parallel across a sinusoidal source: 100 microfarad in series with R, and 0.02 H in series with R](fig:q-gate2016-s1-q54)
', '**Idea used (constant-resistance network):** an R-L branch in parallel with an R-C branch, both with the same R, looks like a pure
resistance $R$ at **every** frequency when $R^2 = \dfrac{L}{C}$.

1. $\dfrac{L}{C} = \dfrac{0.02}{100 \times 10^{-6}} = \dfrac{0.02}{10^{-4}} = 200\ \Omega^2$.
2. $R = \sqrt{200} = 10\sqrt2 \approx 14.14\ \Omega$.

**Why it works:** with $R^2 = L/C$ the admittance $\dfrac{1}{R + j\omega L} + \dfrac{1}{R + \frac{1}{j\omega C}}$ works out to exactly $\dfrac{1}{R}$
for every $\omega$; the reactive parts of the two branches cancel.

**Without a calculator:** $\sqrt{200} = 10\sqrt2 \approx 14.1$. Option C forgets the square root.

**Answer: about 14.14 Ω.**
', 'READY', 'NAT', 14.0, 14.2, 2, 'OFFICIAL_KEY', 'gate2016-s1-q54', 'PYQ') RETURNING id INTO qid;
